      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Distinguishes SaaS, B2B, B2C, hardware, investor, consulting etc.—a genuine axis to segment expansion opportunities. Sampled values are sound readings (consulting for 280 Group, venture_investor for the VC firms, B2C for 23andme)."
    },
    {
      "name": "customer_segment_primary",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Enterprise vs consumer vs developer segmentation is directly relevant to market-expansion targeting. Sampled values are defensible, though VC firms labeled 'enterprise' is a loose fit; still a reasonable categorization and not contradicted."
    },
    {
      "name": "company_stage",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Stage is a useful lens for expansion readiness, but the source descriptions rarely state stage. Labels like 'established_scale' for 23andme and 'growth_stage' for 280 Group appear inferred from outside knowledge rather than derivable from the given text, so groundedness is weak."
    },
    {
      "name": "technology_capability_class",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Provides a useful technical-capability axis, though 'not_present' dominates (114), reducing leverage for the majority of rows. Where values are assigned they are well-grounded (data_management for Addepar, bioscience for 5AM Ventures), and 'not_present' for silent rows is correct behaviour."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.83,
  "source_groundedness": 0.76,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively provide several genuine, non-redundant axes (industry, business model, customer segment, stage, tech capability) that are directly relevant to studying market-expansion focus, giving analysts real grouping and comparison power. Groundedness is generally solid for industry/business-model/customer/tech columns, which read soundly from the descriptions. The main weakness is company_stage, which is frequently inferred beyond what the source text supports, and occasional over-specific vertical labels (e.g., Accel as life_sciences from a generic description)."
